FFmpeg (<http://ffmpeg.org/>), for audio and video, is licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License (LGPL) version 2.1 or later by default, but the
license of a build depends on how it's configured, and a binary which includes
it has the same license:

- Homebrew's FFmpeg includes GPL components, such as x264 and x265, so it's
  licensed under the GNU General Public License (GPL).
- go-media (v1.11.0 or later) builds FFmpeg for GO_MEDIA_PREFIX with
  --enable-gpl and --enable-version3, which FFmpeg reports as "GPL version 3
  or later".
- go-media's FFMPEG_NONFREE=1 adds --enable-nonfree, which FFmpeg reports as
  "nonfree and unredistributable", so a binary built with it can't be
  redistributed.

A binary which includes a GPL build of FFmpeg must be distributed under the
GPL, with its complete source code. The license of a build of go-media's is
FFMPEG_LICENSE in its build/ffmpeg-<version>/config.h.

